   "source": [
    "# Cost Attribution Walkthrough - Vantara Commerce\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides an interactive analysis of AI cost attribution using Briefcase AI. We'll demonstrate how to attribute Vantara Commerce's $3.8M annual AI spend to individual teams, models, and decisions.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Problem Context\n",
    "\n",
    "Vantara Commerce receives aggregate AI bills from 4 vendors:\n",
    "- **OpenAI**: $1.9M annually (GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini)\n",
    "- **Anthropic**: $950K annually (Claude-3-5-Sonnet, Claude-3-Haiku)\n",
    "- **Google Vertex**: $760K annually (Gemini-1.5-Pro, Gemini-1.5-Flash)\n",
    "- **Cohere**: $190K annually (Command-R, Command-R-Plus)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Questions:**\n",
    "- Which teams drive the highest AI costs?\n",
    "- Are premium models justified by their usage patterns?\n",
    "- How much could we save by right-sizing models?\n",
    "- What's the real cost impact of Q4 peak season?\n",
    "\n",
    "## The Briefcase AI Solution\n",
    "\n",
    "Briefcase AI tracks costs at the decision level, enabling precise attribution from individual AI calls up to annual budgets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup and Configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",
    "import random\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add shared module to path\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.join('..', 'shared'))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Import our demo modules\n",
    "import backend\n",
    "from backend import briefcase_ai, COMPANY, VENDOR_PRICING, compute_cost\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set styling for better visualizations\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n",
    "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set deterministic random seed\n",
    "random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Briefcase AI Cost Attribution Demo\")\n",
    "print(f\"Company: {COMPANY['name']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Annual AI Spend: ${COMPANY['annual_ai_spend_estimate_usd']:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Monthly AI Decisions: {COMPANY['monthly_ai_decisions_estimate']:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Peak Season Multiplier: {COMPANY['peak_cost_multiplier']}x\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Display vendor pricing table\n",
    "pricing_data = []\n",
    "for vendor, models in VENDOR_PRICING.items():\n",
    "    for model, (input_price, output_price) in models.items():\n",
    "        pricing_data.append({\n",
    "            'Vendor': vendor,\n",
    "            'Model': model,\n",
    "            'Input Price ($/1M tokens)': f\"${input_price:.2f}\",\n",
    "            'Output Price ($/1M tokens)': f\"${output_price:.2f}\",\n",
    "            'Total (1K in + 1K out)': f\"${(input_price + output_price)/1000:.4f}\"\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "pricing_df = pd.DataFrame(pricing_data)\n",
    "print(\"\\nVendor Pricing Table:\")\n",
    "print(pricing_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize Briefcase AI\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    briefcase_ai.init()\n",
    "    print(\"\\nSUCCESS: Briefcase AI SDK initialized\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nINFO: Using mock implementation ({e})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "backend_instance = backend.get_backend()\n",
    "print(\"SUCCESS: In-memory SQLite backend configured\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cost Calculation Examples\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's demonstrate cost calculation for different scenarios to understand the pricing model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example cost calculations for common scenarios\n",
    "scenarios = [\n",
    "    {\"name\": \"Search Query (Light)\", \"vendor\": \"google-vertex\", \"model\": \"gemini-1.5-flash\", \n",
    "     \"input_tokens\": 200, \"output_tokens\": 50},\n",
    "    {\"name\": \"Product Recommendation\", \"vendor\": \"openai\", \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \n",
    "     \"input_tokens\": 500, \"output_tokens\": 150},\n",
    "    {\"name\": \"Dynamic Pricing (Premium)\", \"vendor\": \"openai\", \"model\": \"gpt-4o\", \n",
    "     \"input_tokens\": 800, \"output_tokens\": 200},\n",
    "    {\"name\": \"Customer Support\", \"vendor\": \"anthropic\", \"model\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet\", \n",
    "     \"input_tokens\": 1200, \"output_tokens\": 400},\n",
    "    {\"name\": \"Batch Processing\", \"vendor\": \"google-vertex\", \"model\": \"gemini-1.5-pro\", \n",
    "     \"input_tokens\": 5000, \"output_tokens\": 1000}\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "cost_examples = []\n",
    "for scenario in scenarios:\n",
    "    input_cost, output_cost = compute_cost(\n",
    "        scenario[\"vendor\"], scenario[\"model\"], \n",
    "        scenario[\"input_tokens\"], scenario[\"output_tokens\"]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    total_cost = input_cost + output_cost\n",
    "    \n",
    "    cost_examples.append({\n",
    "        'Scenario': scenario[\"name\"],\n",
    "        'Model': f\"{scenario['vendor']}/{scenario['model']}\",\n",
    "        'Input Tokens': scenario[\"input_tokens\"],\n",
    "        'Output Tokens': scenario[\"output_tokens\"],\n",
    "        'Input Cost': f\"${input_cost:.6f}\",\n",
    "        'Output Cost': f\"${output_cost:.6f}\",\n",
    "        'Total Cost': f\"${total_cost:.6f}\",\n",
    "        'Cost Numeric': total_cost\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "cost_df = pd.DataFrame(cost_examples)\n",
    "print(\"Cost Calculation Examples:\")\n",
    "print(cost_df.drop('Cost Numeric', axis=1).to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize cost differences\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cost by scenario\n",
    "costs = [example['Cost Numeric'] for example in cost_examples]\n",
    "names = [example['Scenario'] for example in cost_examples]\n",
    "ax1.bar(names, costs, color='skyblue', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Cost per Decision by Use Case')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Cost (USD)')\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Token usage vs cost\n",
    "total_tokens = [ex['Input Tokens'] + ex['Output Tokens'] for ex in cost_examples]\n",
    "ax2.scatter(total_tokens, costs, s=100, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "for i, name in enumerate(names):\n",
    "    ax2.annotate(name.split()[0], (total_tokens[i], costs[i]), \n",
    "                xytext=(5, 5), textcoords='offset points', fontsize=8)\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Token Usage vs Cost')\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel('Total Tokens')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Cost (USD)')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate annual projections\n",
    "print(\"\\nAnnual Cost Projections (at 100K decisions/day):\")\n",
    "for example in cost_examples:\n",
    "    annual_cost = example['Cost Numeric'] * 100_000 * 365\n",
    "    print(f\"  {example['Scenario']:<25}: ${annual_cost:>8,.0f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Running Cost Attribution Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's simulate real cost attribution across Vantara's teams and analyze the results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import and run the cost attribution simulation\n",
    "from example import simulate_cost_attribution_decisions, DECISIONS_CONFIG\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Running cost attribution simulation...\")\n",
    "print(f\"Simulating {len(DECISIONS_CONFIG)} decisions across 10 teams\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate decisions\n",
    "cost_decisions = simulate_cost_attribution_decisions()\n",
    "print(f\"SUCCESS: Generated {len(cost_decisions)} cost-attributed decisions\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Store in backend\n",
    "stored_ids = []\n",
    "for decision in cost_decisions:\n",
    "    decision_id = backend_instance.store_decision(decision)\n",
    "    stored_ids.append(decision_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"SUCCESS: Stored {len(stored_ids)} decisions in audit trail\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract decision data for analysis\n",
    "decision_data = []\n",
    "for decision in cost_decisions:\n",
    "    decision_info = {\n",
    "        'team': decision.inputs[0].value,\n",
    "        'vendor': decision.inputs[1].value,\n",
    "        'model': decision.inputs[2].value,\n",
    "        'request_type': decision.inputs[3].value,\n",
    "        'customer_segment': decision.inputs[4].value,\n",
    "        'input_tokens': int(decision.inputs[5].value),\n",
    "        'output_tokens': int(decision.inputs[6].value),\n",
    "        'timestamp': decision.inputs[7].value,\n",
    "        'use_case_type': decision.inputs[8].value,\n",
    "        'is_peak_season': decision.inputs[9].value == 'True',\n",
    "        'input_cost': float(decision.outputs[0].value),\n",
    "        'output_cost': float(decision.outputs[1].value),\n",
    "        'total_cost': float(decision.outputs[2].value),\n",
    "        'cost_per_decision': float(decision.outputs[3].value),\n",
    "        'decision_id': decision.decision_id\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    decision_info['total_tokens'] = decision_info['input_tokens'] + decision_info['output_tokens']\n",
    "    decision_data.append(decision_info)\n",
    "\n",
    "decisions_df = pd.DataFrame(decision_data)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display summary statistics\n",
    "print(\"COST ATTRIBUTION SUMMARY:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total decisions analyzed: {len(decisions_df)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Teams represented: {decisions_df['team'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total sample cost: ${decisions_df['total_cost'].sum():.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Average cost per decision: ${decisions_df['total_cost'].mean():.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Peak season decisions: {decisions_df['is_peak_season'].sum()} ({decisions_df['is_peak_season'].mean()*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "decisions_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Team-Level Cost Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Analyze costs by team to understand spending patterns and identify optimization opportunities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Team-level analysis\n",
    "team_analysis = decisions_df.groupby(['team', 'vendor', 'model']).agg({\n",
